        <h2>BBS.eonic.cloud — Coming Online</h2>
        <p>
            We're standing up a BBS — a bulletin board system — at
            <strong>bbs.eonic.cloud</strong>, running ENiGMA½ in Docker on Halbox.
            It's the retro-computing community hub that matches the world we build on
            screen: not just a website, but a <em>place</em>.
        </p>
        <div class="connect-box">
            <strong>How to connect (telnet):</strong><br>
            <code>telnet bbs.eonic.cloud 9990</code><br>
            <span style="color:var(--dim);font-size:0.85em;">
            Use any telnet client (macOS/Linux: <code>telnet</code> or <code>nc</code>;
            Windows: SyncTERM or NetRunner for the full ANSI experience). A
            connect-in-your-browser (fTelnet) option is on the way.</span>
        </div>
        <h3>What Will Be On the BBS</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Show notes for every podcast episode</li>
            <li>Downloadable Amiga programs — real executables that run in FS-UAE or on a real Amiga</li>
            <li>IFF image files generated by Ami, our Amiga graphics agent</li>
            <li>Message boards for fans to discuss episodes</li>
            <li>A retro-computing community hub matching the show's aesthetic</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:0.9em;">
            Note: we're finishing the last mile of network setup (DNS is pointed
            straight at the box; the connection port is being opened at the edge). If
            <code>telnet bbs.eonic.cloud 9990</code> doesn't answer yet, check back
            shortly — we're almost there.
        </p>
